# Local configuration. `.env.example` is the template that is committed.
# Render sets VITE_API_URL as a real environment variable at build time and
# Vite gives those priority over .env files, so a stray committed .env would
# not break the deployment — but it would still point a teammate's build at
# localhost, so it stays out of the repository.
.env
.env.local
*.local
.DS_Store
*.log
.vite/
